[C1] PASS the face form conserves E + PE_d exactly on a closed column: max |sum V (W^face + phi drho)| / sum V |W^face| = 3.9e-15 (Cartesian and spherical-polar)
[C2] PASS the cell form leaves an E + PE_d defect equal to sum V (W^cell - W^face); with F = F^R cell mode books no face work: defect / sum V |W^cell| = 1.588e-02; face work of F - F^R: all zero
[C3] PASS the face form's work is second order against the exact cell average, interior and wall cells: orders interior ['2.00', '2.00', '2.00'], wall ['2.00', '2.00', '2.00'] (n = 32..256)
[C4] PASS the curvature flux makes the interior work fourth order, leaves the wall cells first order, and sums to zero over the column: orders interior ['3.94', '3.97', '3.99'], wall ['1.00', '1.00', '1.00']; |sum V div K| / sum V |div K| = 5.0e-17
[C5] PASS face-wallc keeps the cell work in the two wall cells, so its E + PE_d defect is their cell-minus-face work: defect -6.937e-04, wall-cell difference -6.937e-04
